==============================================================================
### 4c. ROTATIONAL INVARIANCE about the NED z (down) axis
==============================================================================
Gravity is along NED +z, so ONLY rotations about z are a symmetry of the
problem. Rotating the whole configuration by psi about z must rotate the
whole trajectory by psi and leave body-frame quantities untouched.

psi = 0.7 rad, 40 s at dt=0.02, aileron+rudder excited
  max |vel_body diff|   = 5.684342e-14 m/s
  max |omega diff|      = 2.498002e-16 rad/s
  max |pos - R pos|     = 6.808477e-09 m
  max |quat - qz*quat|  = 1.831868e-15
  |pos| scale           = 1.219e+04 m

psi = 2.5 rad, 40 s at dt=0.02, aileron+rudder excited
  max |vel_body diff|   = 5.684342e-14 m/s
  max |omega diff|      = 3.261280e-16 rad/s
  max |pos - R pos|     = 1.906119e-08 m
  max |quat - qz*quat|  = 9.992007e-16
  |pos| scale           = 1.219e+04 m

psi = -1.9 rad, 40 s at dt=0.02, aileron+rudder excited
  max |vel_body diff|   = 1.705303e-13 m/s
  max |omega diff|      = 3.747003e-16 rad/s
  max |pos - R pos|     = 1.398314e-08 m
  max |quat - qz*quat|  = 3.913536e-15
  |pos| scale           = 1.219e+04 m

-- control: a rotation about NED x (NOT a symmetry, gravity is along z) --
  max |vel_body diff| = 9.197289e+00 m/s   <- expected to be LARGE; this is the control that the test above is not vacuous

